<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block">
  <!--
    WildcardFieldResolution.mml
    Wildcard capture → field/key lookup → vector projection → VectorLane scoring → bound result.

    Content dictionary: urn:kuhul:wildcard-field-resolution:v1
    Upstream contracts:
      XaimlMicronautDispatch.mml  — wildcard capture binding (BindingGap, TypedBindings)
      GMLTopology.mml             — FieldParamRecord (four read-only parameter vectors)
      vectors.mml                 — VectorMuMicronaut::ExecuteProjection, MicronautAttraction
    Lane grammar: drivers/grammar/ebnf/21-lanes.ebnf  (<vector-lane>)
    XCFE program: xcfe.aiml-micronaut-dispatch.json   (Sek sync step on lane_set)

    AUTHORITY BOUNDARY: field GML parameter values can guide matching and ranking.
    They do not establish semantic truth and do not authorize a route.
    A high VectorLane score is evidence only — XCFE/Ch'en/Xul remain the authority chain.
    Provenance must be carried on every bound result so the authority chain can assess it.

    GML role distinction (invariant from GMLTopology.mml):
      FieldParamRecord GMLs — read-only parameter vectors, no graph relationships:
        entropy_gradient_field.gml  — EntropyDiffusion constants (Omega gate thresholds)
        tensor_field.gml            — Riemannian metric tensor g_ij, Riemann curvature
        quantum_field_boundaries.gml — wave physics (wave_number, refractive, amplitude)
        euclidean_gradient_field.gml — conservative gradient (curl=0, scalar_potential)
      Topology GMLs — graph relationships, no cbuffer role:
        unfold-graph.gml, khanary_topology.gml, hypercube_Q3/Q4.gml, ccc_n3/n4.gml, metric_graph.gml
    The two roles must not be collapsed: a topology GML does not supply parameter vectors
    and a FieldParamRecord GML does not supply adjacency.
  -->

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>SyncActivation</mi>
      <mo>:</mo>
      <mi>Wo</mi>
      <mo>&#x22A2;</mo>
      <mi>lane_set</mi>
      <mo>,</mo>
      <mspace width="0.5em"/>
      <mi>Sek</mi>
      <mo>&#x22A2;</mo>
      <mi>field_call</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:wildcard-field-resolution:v1">SyncActivation</csymbol>
        <ci>Wo_bind</ci>
        <ci>lane_set_declaration</ci>
        <ci>Sek_sync</ci>
        <ci>field_call_execution</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
SyncActivation: the field is called at Sek sync, not at Wo bind.
  Wo  (op: bind,  id: lane_set,  type: pattern_sync_decls):
      declares which lanes are accessible from the static &lt;xaiml:sync&gt; declarations.
      lane_set is a declared set — no field is called, no parameter resolved.
  Sek (op: sync,  id: lane_set):
      activates each declared lane. For every VectorLane entry in lane_set, THIS is
      the field call: the WildcardFieldResolution pipeline runs at this step.
      For every NGramLane entry, GramStore lookup runs. For FieldLane, relation query runs.
      The sync step is the dispatch boundary between "declared accessible" and "actually called."
XCFE program reference: xcfe.aiml-micronaut-dispatch.json step 9 (phase Sek, op sync, id lane_set).
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>WildcardFieldPipeline</mi>
      <mo>:</mo>
      <mi>capture</mi>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo>
      <mi>FieldKeyLookup</mi>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo>
      <mi>VectorProjection</mi>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo>
      <mi>VectorLaneScore</mi>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo>
      <mi>BoundResult</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>provenance</mi><mo>)</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:wildcard-field-resolution:v1">WildcardFieldPipeline</csymbol>
        <ci>capture</ci>
        <ci>FieldKeyLookup</ci>
        <ci>VectorProjection</ci>
        <ci>VectorLaneScore</ci>
        <ci>BoundResult</ci>
        <ci>provenance</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
WildcardFieldPipeline: five-stage pipeline, triggered at Sek sync for each VectorLane in lane_set.
  Stage 1 — capture:        AIML * wildcard produces a typed binding (phrase/entity/predicate/identifier).
                            Bound at Wo; available to the pipeline when sync fires at Sek.
  Stage 2 — FieldKeyLookup: capture key is matched against FieldParamRecord GML node labels / attributes.
                            Result: a parameter vector from the matching GML file (read-only).
  Stage 3 — VectorProjection: VectorMuMicronaut::ExecuteProjection() projects the capture against
                            the resolved parameter vector. Returns a bounded result substrate.
  Stage 4 — VectorLaneScore: the projection result is scored via the &lt;vector-lane&gt; (21-lanes.ebnf,
                            capability="vector-score"). Score ∈ [0,1]; no topology mutation.
  Stage 5 — BoundResult:    score + resolved parameter vector + source GML filename are packaged
                            as a bound result with source provenance.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>FieldKeyLookup</mi>
      <mo>(</mo><mi>capture</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo>
      <mo>&#x7B;</mo>
      <mi>file</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>param_vector</mi>
      <mo>&#x7D;</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:wildcard-field-resolution:v1">FieldKeyLookup</csymbol>
        <list>
          <list><ci>entropy</ci><ci>ambiguity</ci><ci>diffusion</ci></list>
          <ci>entropy_gradient_field.gml</ci>
          <list><ci>entropy_bound</ci><ci>diffusion_beta_inv</ci><ci>entropy_spike</ci></list>
        </list>
        <list>
          <list><ci>curvature</ci><ci>metric</ci><ci>tensor</ci><ci>bundle</ci></list>
          <ci>tensor_field.gml</ci>
          <list><ci>g_00</ci><ci>g_01</ci><ci>g_10</ci><ci>g_11</ci><ci>riemann_curvature_scalar</ci><ci>jacobian_w</ci></list>
        </list>
        <list>
          <list><ci>wave</ci><ci>boundary</ci><ci>refractive</ci><ci>frequency</ci></list>
          <ci>quantum_field_boundaries.gml</ci>
          <list><ci>wave_number</ci><ci>refractive</ci><ci>amplitude_re</ci><ci>amplitude_im</ci><ci>phase_shift</ci></list>
        </list>
        <list>
          <list><ci>gradient</ci><ci>potential</ci><ci>conservative</ci><ci>path</ci></list>
          <ci>euclidean_gradient_field.gml</ci>
          <list><ci>scalar_potential</ci><ci>arc_length</ci><ci>curl</ci><ci>potential_delta</ci></list>
        </list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
FieldKeyLookup: capture key term → GML file → parameter vector (read-only).
Lookup is by semantic key family, not exact string match. Canonical mappings:
  {entropy, ambiguity, diffusion}   → entropy_gradient_field.gml
      param vector: {entropy_bound=4.00, diffusion_beta_inv=0.25, entropy_spike threshold}
      use: guides Omega gate threshold — high local_entropy (3.82) vs low (0.15) contrast.
  {curvature, metric, tensor, bundle} → tensor_field.gml
      param vector: {g_00=-0.8524, g_01=0.0125, g_11=1.1486, riemann_curvature_scalar=-0.412, jacobian_w=1.0834}
      use: non-Euclidean local metric for parallel transport scoring; negative curvature = hyperbolic region.
  {wave, boundary, refractive, freq} → quantum_field_boundaries.gml
      param vector: {wave_number=2.1/1.4, refractive=1.0/3.4, amplitude_re/im, phase_shift=π/4, π/2}
      use: wave-propagation matching — refractive index 3.4 signals a high-impedance boundary reset.
  {gradient, potential, conservative, path} → euclidean_gradient_field.gml
      param vector: {scalar_potential ∈ [0.20, 0.95], arc_length=2.8284, curl=0, potential_delta=0.75}
      use: conservative path scoring — curl=0 proves no holonomy; potential_delta ranks ascent.
Lookup miss (capture key matches no family) → DATA_ONLY return; no projection attempted.
Multiple matches → score each resolved vector; provenance must list all source files.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>VectorLaneScore</mi>
      <mo>:</mo>
      <mi>mode</mi>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <mi>score</mi>
      <mo>,</mo>
      <mspace width="0.5em"/>
      <mi>mutation_authorized</mi>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <mi>false</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:wildcard-field-resolution:v1">VectorLaneScoringLaw</csymbol>
        <ci>vector-lane</ci>
        <ci>score</ci>
        <false/>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
VectorLaneScoringLaw: the VectorLane operates in mode="score" for field-resolved projections.
  Lane type: VectorLane (21-lanes.ebnf), capability="vector-score".
  The projection result substrate from ExecuteProjection() feeds the lane's &lt;score_result&gt; element.
  mutation_authorized="false" — the parameter vector from FieldParamRecord GMLs is read-only.
  No topology node, edge, or gram entry is created or modified by a VectorLane score pass.
  The score is carried forward as a WCR input (weights matching and ranking) at Yax,
  not as a capability grant or route authorization.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>BoundResult</mi>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <mo>&#x27E8;</mo>
      <mi>score</mi>
      <mo>,</mo>
      <mi>param_vector</mi>
      <mo>,</mo>
      <mi>source_gml</mi>
      <mo>,</mo>
      <mi>semantic_authority</mi>
      <mo>=</mo>
      <mi>false</mi>
      <mo>&#x27E9;</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:wildcard-field-resolution:v1">BoundResultWithProvenance</csymbol>
        <ci>score</ci>
        <ci>param_vector</ci>
        <ci>source_gml</ci>
        <false/>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
BoundResultWithProvenance: every result from this pipeline is a 4-tuple.
  score        — numeric score from VectorLane (∈ [0,1]); used as WCR ranking input.
  param_vector — the resolved parameter constants from the source GML (read-only snapshot).
  source_gml   — filename of the FieldParamRecord GML that supplied the parameters.
                 Required for authority chain assessment: Ch'en can inspect provenance.
  semantic_authority=false — field GML parameter values do not establish semantic truth.
                 A score of 1.0 from entropy_gradient_field.gml does not prove a semantic claim.
                 It does not authorize a route. XCFE/Ch'en/Xul remain the authority chain.
Provenance is mandatory — a BoundResult without source_gml is malformed and must be rejected
before it reaches the Yax W·C·R gate.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>ScoringNotTruth</mi>
      <mo>:</mo>
      <mi>score</mi>
      <mo>&#x2208;</mo>
      <mo>[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo>
      <mo>&#x21CF;</mo>
      <mi>semantic_authority</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:wildcard-field-resolution:v1">ScoringNotTruth</csymbol>
        <ci>score</ci>
        <ci>semantic_authority</ci>
        <ci>route_authorization</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
ScoringNotTruth: field GML scores are evidence, not truth.
  score ∈ [0,1] does not imply semantic_authority.
  score ∈ [0,1] does not authorize a route.
  A capture resolving to tensor_field.gml parameters produces a curvature-guided score.
  That score can rank candidates at Yax; it cannot make a topology commit at Xul.
  The authority chain is strictly:
    field GML lookup → score (evidence) → W·C·R Yax gate → Ch'en verification → Xul commit.
  No step in this pipeline may bypass or pre-empt a later gate.
  Epistemic status of a BoundResult: SUPPORTED (if score meets threshold) or MISS (if lookup fails).
  Never CONTRADICTED by a score alone — CONTRADICTED requires Ch'en verification of conflicting evidence.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <annotation encoding="text/plain">
WildcardFieldResolution contract invariants:
1. SyncActivation: Wo bind declares lane_set (accessible); Sek sync calls the field (executed).
   The pipeline triggers at Sek sync, not at Wo bind. Captures are available at sync time.
2. Pipeline is five stages: capture → FieldKeyLookup → VectorProjection → VectorLaneScore → BoundResult.
   All five stages execute within the Sek sync step for each VectorLane in lane_set.
3. FieldKeyLookup is read-only: FieldParamRecord GMLs supply parameter vectors; no writes.
4. Topology GMLs (unfold-graph, hypercube_Q3/Q4, ccc, khanary_topology, metric_graph) are not
   consulted in this pipeline — they provide graph relationships, not parameter vectors.
5. VectorLane mode="score" for this pipeline; mutation_authorized=false.
6. Every BoundResult carries source_gml provenance. A result without provenance is malformed.
7. Scores guide W·C·R matching and ranking at Yax. They are evidence, not semantic truth.
8. A field GML score cannot authorize a route; XCFE/Ch'en/Xul remain the authority chain.
9. Lookup miss → DATA_ONLY. Multiple matches → score each; list all source files in provenance.
  </annotation>
</math>
